      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T16:58:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(posting): re-derive the standing-steel swing on #818's level lines\n\nMerge upstream/main (#818: the index swing is judged about any level\nline, and from the WCS origin for stacked rotaries) and rebuild the\n#1107 clause on its Verdict/index_angle/swept API instead of the\nremoved A-about-X `work_a`:\n\n- one level line u: the work's span is taken along u, a fixed fixture\n  beside that span is clear, else its (s, z) box distance from the\n  line (s along u x Z) is judged - exact for X and Y, a lower bound\n  (refuses more, never clears falsely) off both;\n- stacked rotaries: fixed fixtures are judged by box distance from the\n  WCS origin against the sweep about it; the face under them is named\n  not judged;\n- swept() now returns the radius and the span along the line.\n\nPinned by a_table_b_judges_the_work_against_standing_steel_about_y,\nan_a_stated_level_but_off_x_judges_standing_steel_about_its_own_line,\nstacked_rotaries_judge_standing_steel_from_the_wcs_origin_and_name_the_face\nand the end-face touch in\na_standing_fixture_under_the_work_is_judged_by_its_distance_from_the_line.\n\nRefs #1107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
